1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,000
In 2012, NASA's fire record jumped.

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,200
The fires didn't change.
The satellite did.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:10,300
Zij joins MODIS and VIIRS
into one record, 2000 to today.

4
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:13,800
Tested on unseen years:
error falls from 77% to 14%.

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,000
Draw any area and ask:
is this fire season normal?

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,900
See any day's fires
over NASA satellite imagery.

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,900
Download every number.
Plan, warn, respond.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:29,300
1,000 years ago, a zij charted the sky.
Ours charts a safer Earth.
